'''Kurupiran-Nyengatú''' (/ku.ɾu.piˈɾãn ɲẽ.ɡaˈtú/; {{Audio|Bl-Kurupiran-Nyengatú.mp3|pronunciation}}) is the most widely distributed subfamily of the [[Kurupiran languages]] of [[Abyala]]. It consists of about fifty languages, including [[Old Kurupiran]] and [[Nyengatú language|Nyengatú]]. The most widely spoken in modern times by far is Nyengatú, which is one of the X official languages of [[Pindorama]].

The words ''[[W:Petunia|petunia]], [[W:Jaguar|jaguar]], [[W:Piranha|piranha]], [[W:Ipecac|ipecac]], [[W:Tapioca|tapioca]], [[W:Jacaranda|jacaranda]], [[W:Anhinga|anhinga]], [[W:Carioca|carioca]]'', and ''[[W:Capoeira|capoeira]]'' are of Kurupiran-Nyengatú origin.

